---

<Layout title="Drylining Musselburgh | Partition Walls &amp; Ceilings Contractors" description="Professional drylining contractors in Musselburgh. Expert partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation for Musselburgh, East Lothian, and the wider EH postcode region. Free quotes." canonical="/areas/musselburgh/" schema={schema}>
  <section style="position:relative;min-height:400px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e 0%,#16213e 100%);overflow:hidden;"> <img src="/images/hero-main.jpg" alt="Drylining services in Musselburgh and East Lothian" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;opacity:0.25;"> <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;padding:60px 20px;"> <nav style="font-size:13px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);margin-bottom:12px;"> <a href="/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Home</a> / <a href="/areas/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Areas</a> / <span style="color:#ffffff;">Drylining in Musselburgh</span> </nav> <h1 style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);font-weight:800;color:#ffffff;margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.15;">Drylining in Musselburgh</h1> <p style="font-size:17px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.6;">CSCS-accredited drylining contractors delivering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard across Musselburgh, East Lothian, and the wider EH21 postcode region.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;"> <div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);"> <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Drylining Musselburgh provides drylining, partition walls, and suspended ceilings across Musselburgh (EH21), East Lothian, and the wider council area. Experienced with historic burgh properties, new build estates, and commercial fit-outs across East Lothian.</p> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Drylining Services in Musselburgh</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Musselburgh is East Lothian's largest town with a population of around 21,000 residents in the EH21 postcode area. Home to the famous Musselburgh Racecourse, the River Esk estuary, and one of Scotland's oldest burghs, the area offers a unique mix of historic properties, modern residential developments, and coastal commercial sites. This diversity means our drylining contractors work on everything from historic property restorations around the town centre and racecourse to new build developments along the A6110 corridor and coastal regeneration zones.</p> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Musselburgh's ongoing regeneration projects — including the town centre improvements, the River Esk waterfront developments, and the A6110 corridor enhancements — create consistent demand for commercial drylining services. We deliver partition wall installation, suspended ceilings, and fire-rated wall systems for office refurbishments, retail units, healthcare premises, and residential developments throughout the EH21 postcode area. All work is carried out to Scottish Building Standards Part H and Part T standards.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What We Do in Musselburgh</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our Musselburgh crew handles everything from single-room domestic renovations on King Street to large-scale commercial fit-outs around the Racecourse — covering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation across the entire EH21 postcode region.</p> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><strong>Period property drylining</strong> — Internal wall insulation, room conversions, and partition walls in historic burgh properties and listed buildings around King Street and the Racecourse area</li> <li><strong>New build handover drylining</strong> — Pre-completion drylining for housing developments in Easthouses, Macmerry, and the Musselburgh town centre regeneration zones</li> <li><strong>Commercial fit-outs</strong> — Office refurbs, retail units, and restaurant conversions along King Street, the Racecourse area, and the A6110 corridor</li> <li><strong>Fire-rated walls</strong> — Multi-storey residential and commercial buildings require Scottish Building Standards compliance, delivered with full documentation for East Lothian Council building standards</li> <li><strong>Suspended ceilings</strong> — Office refurbs, healthcare premises, and education facilities throughout the Musselburgh and East Lothian area</li> <li><strong>Acoustic partitions</strong> — Residential blocks, student accommodation, and hotel conversions near the Racecourse hotels and East Lothian's hospitality sector</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Areas of Musselburgh We Cover</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li>Musselburgh town centre and King Street (EH21)</li> <li>Racecourse and Eastfield (EH21)</li> <li>Easthouses (EH21)</li> <li>Macmerry (EH21)</li> <li>Dunglass (EH21)</li> <li>Gogar and South Gullane (EH21)</li> <li>Rainworth and Ormiston (EH22)</li> <li>Pencaitland and Haddington (EH41)</li> <li>Tranent and Wallyford (EH33)</li> <li>Gorebridge and Borthwick (EH26)</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Musselburgh Building Standards &amp; Planning</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Musselburgh falls under <strong>East Lothian Council</strong> for building standards and planning. The town contains several listed buildings, particularly in the historic town centre and near the Racecourse conservation areas. Many properties are within designated <strong>Musselburgh Conservation Areas</strong>, meaning any internal structural alterations or external drylining insulation may require listed building consent or planning permission. We work closely with clients, architects, and the council building standards surveyors to ensure every project — from a simple room partition in a Georgian house on King Street to a large commercial fit-out around the Racecourse — is fully compliant with current Scottish Building Standards.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Us for Musselburgh Projects</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">As a Musselburgh-based drylining team with daily operations across East Lothian, we understand the town's unique demands. From managing access on the A6110 corridor to working around the Racecourse's event schedules and the coastal environment's moisture concerns, our crew knows the area inside out. All operatives are DBS checked, fully uniformed, and experienced in delivering quality work in Musselburgh's historic and coastal environments.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Related Services</h2> <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <a href="/services/partition-walls/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Partition Walls</a> <a href="/services/fire-rated-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Fire-Rated Drylining</a> <a href="/services/acoustic-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Acoustic Drylining</a> <a href="/services/refurbishment-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Refurbishment Drylining</a> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Nearby Areas</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><a href="/areas/edinburgh/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Edinburgh</a> — 10 minutes via A6110</li> <li><a href="/areas/dalkeith/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Dalkeith</a> — 10 minutes via A68</li> <li><a href="/areas/peebles/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Peebles</a> — 35 minutes via A7</li> <li><a href="/areas/livingston/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Livingston</a> — 40 minutes via M8</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2> <div style="margin-bottom:2rem;"> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> What is dry lining and how does it work? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Dry lining is a method of finishing internal walls and ceilings with plasterboard rather than applying several layers of wet plaster. The boards can be fixed directly to brick or blockwork with drywall adhesive, often called the dot and dab method, or screwed to a timber or metal frame. Once the plasterboard is secure, the joints and screw heads are covered with tape and jointing compound. The surface can then be sanded, painted, wallpapered or finished with a thin plaster skim. Dry lining is commonly used in new builds, extensions, renovations and commercial properties. It provides a smooth finish quickly and can also create space for insulation, soundproofing materials, electrical cables and pipework. </div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> Do I need planning permission for drylining in Musselburgh? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Internal drylining usually falls under permitted development rights and doesn't require planning permission. However, if your property is listed (Musselburgh has several listed buildings in the historic town centre and near the Racecourse) or within a Conservation Area, you'll need listed building consent for any internal alterations. We advise checking with East Lothian Council's planning department before starting work on period properties.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> What are Scottish Building Standards for drylining? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Scottish Building Standards Part H covers heat and energy efficiency, Part T covers ventilation, and Part C covers structural adequacy. All our drylining work in Musselburgh complies with current Scottish Building Standards. For fire-rated walls, we follow the Fire Standard (Part B) and provide full documentation. We also ensure thermal insulation meets the latest Part H requirements, which is particularly important for Musselburgh's older properties with solid stone walls.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> How long does drylining take in Musselburgh? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> A typical single-room drylining job takes 2–3 days for framing and board installation, plus 1–2 days for taping, jointing, and sanding. Larger commercial projects around the Racecourse or along the A6110 corridor can take 1–4 weeks depending on scale. We work efficiently to minimise disruption, especially around race days when traffic management is a consideration.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> Do you offer free quotes for Musselburgh projects? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Yes, we offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Musselburgh and East Lothian. We'll assess your property, discuss your requirements, and provide a detailed written quote within 48 hours. Call us on 0800 820 3090 or fill in our contact form to arrange your free site visit.</div> </details> </div> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Get a Free Musselburgh Quote</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem;">We offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Musselburgh. Call us or fill in our quick form.</p> <div style="margin-top:2rem;text-align:center;"> <a href="/get-quote/" class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;">Get a Free Musselburgh Quote</a> <a href="tel:08008203090" class="btn btn-secondary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;border:2px solid var(--primary);background:transparent;color:var(--primary);margin-left:0.5rem;">FREEPHONE 0800 820 3090</a> </div> </div></section>
</Layout>
